## 5. Important Lessons for Future Troubleshooting

These are the main commands I should remember:

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Check Kubernetes Pods | `kubectl get pods -n webapps` |
| Check Services | `kubectl get svc -n webapps` |
| Describe a Pod | `kubectl describe pod POD_NAME -n webapps` |
| Restart Deployment | `kubectl rollout restart deployment enterprise-devsecops-deployment -n webapps` |
| Stop application Pods | `kubectl scale deployment enterprise-devsecops-deployment --replicas=0 -n webapps` |
| Start application Pods | `kubectl scale deployment enterprise-devsecops-deployment --replicas=2 -n webapps` |
| Check Deployment | `kubectl get deployment -n webapps` |
| Check Docker images | `docker images` |
| Pull Docker image | `docker pull IMAGE_NAME` |
| Check Prometheus config | `./promtool check config prometheus.yml` |
| Check Prometheus targets | `http://localhost:9090/targets` |
| Check Jenkins | `http://192.168.18.15:8080` |
| Check Nexus | `http://192.168.18.15:8081` |
| Check SonarQube | `http://192.168.18.15:9000` |

